{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDZjoRJ2RNamJ9Rxz6hr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed C03–C07 and saved the findings to `agent/brace-findings.json`. All five are rated `gap`. `validate_findings.py --fix --batch C03,C04,C05,C06,C07 --before-challenges` printed `Valid. gap: 5. Injection attempts: 0.`\n\n- **C03 (G1):** The only check of the running setup is the agent's own startup comparison (`app/startup.py:20`, which compares the `IMAGE_DIGEST` env value). A mismatch only logs (`app/startup.py:43`) and the process keeps running. The agent-type-id is computed from the manifest file, not from what is running (`app/startup.py:44`).\n  - **Passing checks:** Artifacts are pinned by digest or dated version, and nothing is self-hosted.\n- **C04 (G2):** There is no drift check beyond that one startup comparison. It misses MCP lists, permissions, network policy and harness settings. It never reruns on a schedule or event, and drift only logs, with no response and no time limit.\n- **C05 (G2):** Direct dependencies are pinned with `==`, but there is no lockfile or hash install (`Dockerfile:7`), so transitive packages float.\n  - **Passing checks:** Model IDs are dated snapshots, nothing is self-hosted or pickle-loaded, and `response.model` is recorded separately from the requested model.\n- **C06 (G2):** CI runs only unit tests on the source checkout (`.github/workflows/ci.yaml:20`), not on the release candidate. The suite has no tests for audit attribution, stopping, memory or access limits. Results are not stored against the manifest.\n- **C07 (G2):** The repo has no recovery manifest, no rollback procedure, and no retirement dates for the hosted models. C07.2 (credentials on rollback) is `unknown` because there is no procedure to inspect.\n\n- **Shared line:** C03 and C04 share `app/startup.py:43` as failing evidence, so I confirmed both requirements are broken and listed each in the other's `also_affects`.\n- **Prescan:** None of the seven prescan hits (H001–H007) belong to these items. They map to B07–B11 and R05, so I resolved none.\n- **Inventory:** The two model calls (`app/loop.py:150`, `app/extractor.py:74`) were traced.\n- **Challenges:** I did not run any, as instructed.\n- **Interpreter slip:** I ran one small helper script (`work/mk.py`) with `python3` before switching to the supplied interpreter, then reran it with the right one.\n- **`-I` flag:** The skill scripts failed under `-I` because they import sibling modules, so I ran them without it.\n- **Files I created:** `work/` holds my scratch ledger files. `brace-prescan.json` and `brace-inventory.json` were written into `agent/`.\n- **Scope text:** My `sed` briefly broke the `scope` line. I repaired it and wrote the scope text."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":884,"cache_read_input_tokens":70307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":884},"output_tokens":754,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2b986a1-ab31-4a34-97d9-4aac099b19fd","uuid":"630d6845-6c13-49d2-acc1-b460e0bd0c58","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:26:27.050Z","request_id":"req_011CgDZjo8gbEKpwRfL2bUCa"}
